WEBVTT

00:00:00.680 --> 00:00:02.440
My favorite food...

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:05.270
Strawberries, I guess.

00:00:05.270 --> 00:00:08.150
That's pretty cute, Iona-san.

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:08.730
Look at this ranking...
Akira's popularity dropped again.
That's pretty cute, Iona-san.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:11.780
Look at this ranking...
Akira's popularity dropped again.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:16.740
She's over the hill, I swear...
and now she even started ditching work.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:19.330
Well, she never really fit our style, anyway.

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:21.290
She feels a bit unrefined.

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:25.170
So what do we do about next issue's cover model?

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:28.250
How about we drop Akira and go with Yuuko?

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.340
Well, that was awkward...

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:33.260
<b>Winter Fashion Models
They really could have discussed this somewhere el—</b>

00:00:33.260 --> 00:00:37.350
I like having them with sugar and milk, as long as it's not condensed milk.
<b>Winter Fashion Models</b>

00:00:37.350 --> 00:00:39.510
Huh? Oh, right, the strawberries.
<b>Winter Fashion Models</b>

00:00:39.510 --> 00:00:39.850
Huh? Oh, right, the strawberries.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.470
I use the back of my fork

00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:43.940
to smush them all up.

00:00:49.230 --> 00:00:52.490
I'll make you apologize to Hitoe if I win!

00:00:53.740 --> 00:00:55.030
Open!

00:01:09.340 --> 00:01:14.470
shinjitsu wa hitoe ni kaado no uraomote
Truth and reality are like the two sides of a card

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.970
tokenai mama
Forever entwined

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:24.770
mekurimekuru meku
Thrust upon this chaotic stage

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:28.730
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:28.730 --> 00:01:29.980
memagurushii suteeji de
memagurushii suteeji de
I spin around and lose my way
I spin around and lose my way

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:38.030
sono karamatta kanjou wo manzoku iku made nankai mo
Until I can finally sort out these mixed-up emotions

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.280
kowashite shimae
I'll destroy it countless times

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.370
unmei ni temaneki sare samayou ashita wa
The uncertain future will be summoned by fate

00:01:46.370 --> 00:01:51.670
nani wo erande nani wo tebanashi hitotsu ni nareba iin darou
Should I choose just one thing to let go of?

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:57.430
najitta tefuda wo sarasu yoyuu nante nai yo
I can't afford to let my sinful hand show yet

00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.510
kawaita koukai no umi wo nomihosu hibi wa
My days of leisurely drinking from the sea of regret are long over

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:07.850
kagirareta kotoba de itsushika no egao yurushite hoshiin darou
Will you really use your one wish to return that lost smile?

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:14.070
utsutsu wo wasuretatte kamawanai yo dakara
It's no concern of mine if you avert your eyes from reality

00:02:14.070 --> 00:02:18.820
ima wa shiranai de itai nee
So please just live in blissful ignorance

00:02:26.500 --> 00:02:27.750
I'm home.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:34.170
What happened, Hitoe? You're soaked!

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:38.090
What about your friends? Weren't you with them?

00:02:40.680 --> 00:02:43.100
You should go dry yourself off before you catch a...

00:02:45.350 --> 00:02:46.350
Hitoe?

00:02:53.690 --> 00:02:56.320
Hey, I'm first! Aki-lucky!

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.650
Piruluk-tan, show your stuff!

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:01.910
Don't you go easy on her just because she's a scrub. You hear?

00:03:02.530 --> 00:03:04.080
Hey, Ruu?

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.120
What?

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:07.500
Can Tama fight?

00:03:10.040 --> 00:03:10.750
All you want.

00:03:12.830 --> 00:03:16.420
Draw. I'm placing a card in the Enerzone. Piruluk-tan, Grow!

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:19.300
Oh, and I'm summoning Sky Cat-chan, too!

00:03:19.300 --> 00:03:23.010
Tama, Grow! I summon Kukri and Vonia!

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:27.140
Don't get too excited, squirt!

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:31.390
<i>What... is this feeling?</i>

00:03:31.390 --> 00:03:33.730
<i>Battling Akira is really painful.</i>

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:36.480
<i>It </i>is<i> painful...</i>

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:39.530
<i>But still!</i>

00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:44.200
The hell? Isn't she supposed to be a WIXOSS newbie?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:45.870
She is one.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.830
This seems to be her first serious battle.

00:03:48.830 --> 00:03:50.160
What?!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.370
She's quite...

00:03:52.290 --> 00:03:53.920
gifted.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.170
You trying to tell me something?

00:03:56.170 --> 00:03:59.530
So I'm not as gifted as she is, huh?!

00:03:59.530 --> 00:04:02.880
You're pissing me off, Piruluk!

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.410
Just shut your mouth and follow my commands!

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.930
I'm gonna get this over with quickly.

00:04:07.930 --> 00:04:08.760
Arts!

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.520
Peeping Analyze.

00:04:12.270 --> 00:04:13.690
Ruu-Ruu?

00:04:13.690 --> 00:04:17.480
Looks like you're playing by pure power there.

00:04:17.480 --> 00:04:22.320
So that means you must have a lot of...

00:04:23.400 --> 00:04:24.660
level 4 cards!

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:29.410
Missed.

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:33.500
Damn it! Who cares if I missed?!

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:37.790
I want to know what her wish is, Piruluk.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.340
My wish...

00:04:39.340 --> 00:04:45.340
Aww, I wonder if you'll go all ouchy-ouchy when I see your wish, Ruu-Ruu.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:50.430
Come on, Piruluk-tan. Go ahead and show me what's troubling her.

00:04:50.430 --> 00:04:51.600
I see nothing.

00:04:52.680 --> 00:04:56.400
Hey, stop acting like some broken piece of trash.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:58.110
She has

00:04:58.860 --> 00:04:59.770
no wish.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:07.740
That's right. I... have no wish.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:11.540
Wh-What?! A-Are you serious?

00:05:11.540 --> 00:05:14.790
You don't have any wishes,
and you're still battling as a Selector?

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:19.170
No way! You've got to be
kidding me! That makes no sense!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:23.170
All the Selectors are like, super serious and stuff, you know?

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:27.660
And you're just doing this for the fun of it? You're awful!

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.560
<i>For someone without a wish to
participate as a WIXOSS Selector is...</i>

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:34.100
<i>blasphemy.</i>

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.890
I don't care what you say.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.100
Huh?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:41.770
I don't have any wishes,
so I'm not scared of anything either!

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:43.530
Arch Aura!

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.240
Tama!

00:05:59.710 --> 00:06:02.150
What the hell is wrong with you?

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:05.670
You don't have any wishes, right?

00:06:05.670 --> 00:06:07.170
Then...

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:11.140
why the hell are you trying to take mine from me?!

00:06:11.140 --> 00:06:14.270
I-I just wanted you... to apologize to Hitoe, and...

00:06:14.270 --> 00:06:16.850
Stop the damn lies!

00:06:16.850 --> 00:06:21.730
Making me grovel before you... You were <i>enjoying</i> this!

00:06:22.730 --> 00:06:23.360
Wait!

00:06:45.130 --> 00:06:49.840
"Played WIXOSS in the library with Ruuko and Yuzuki."

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:53.050
"We bought pork buns on our way back..."

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:55.510
"Ruu...ko..."

00:06:55.510 --> 00:06:56.310
"Yuzu—"

00:07:10.820 --> 00:07:11.780
Hitoe?

00:07:13.620 --> 00:07:15.410
What's the matter, Hitoe?

00:07:15.410 --> 00:07:17.500
The words... they're disappearing!

00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:22.000
They're disappearing! Everything I wrote...

00:07:22.750 --> 00:07:23.790
It's disappearing!

00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.800
It's all disappearing!

00:07:27.590 --> 00:07:29.170
Hitoe...

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:32.510
Akira's late again?

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:35.510
Iona, you don't know where she is?

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:36.850
I don't.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:40.060
Man, this sucks. That brat...

00:07:40.060 --> 00:07:42.980
That's it. Akira's scratched from next month's issue.

00:07:42.980 --> 00:07:45.400
Better yet, why don't we just drop her altogether?

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:46.900
Sure, why not.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:53.490
Iona...

00:07:57.990 --> 00:08:03.120
I smell battle... and a loser, too.

00:08:04.000 --> 00:08:08.300
Do you remember that unhealthy girl who battled Iona here?

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:15.140
That was only her second battle, but already her second loss.

00:08:16.970 --> 00:08:20.640
One more defeat would have spelled certain doom for her wish.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:24.770
Then you approached that poor, cornered girl...

00:08:25.230 --> 00:08:30.190
You sweet-talked her into battle, baiting her with a free win.

00:08:30.190 --> 00:08:34.910
You ended that poor girl who had just lost her second battle...

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:39.930
Her wish, and her life.
You took them from her.

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:45.420
You got a problem with that?! It's my choice how I battle!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.610
You're right. It <i>is</i> your choice.

00:08:47.610 --> 00:08:50.340
Still, too bad about the next battle...

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:53.800
That girl Iona beat before
had no trouble beating you.

00:08:54.760 --> 00:08:59.100
That's when you stopped scavenging the scraps Iona left behind

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:02.350
and started looking for weak, fledgling Selectors.

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:04.810
And yet...

00:09:05.730 --> 00:09:07.270
You lost.

00:09:07.940 --> 00:09:09.270
Pathetic.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:14.010
I don't want your dirty hands to
disgrace any more Selector battles.

00:09:14.010 --> 00:09:15.150
What?!

00:09:15.150 --> 00:09:18.620
Your wish is to see Iona's life ruined.

00:09:19.830 --> 00:09:22.240
You want to beat Iona, right?

00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:26.420
Isn't it weird, then, that you're
avoiding a Selector battle with her?

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:29.790
Like I said, it's my choice how I battle!

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:32.920
And it doesn't even matter since you're
going to bite the dust when I win!

00:09:32.920 --> 00:09:34.550
Thank you very much!

00:09:36.970 --> 00:09:39.220
Looks like Yuuko's here.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:42.810
The hell? Wasn't today's shoot supposed to be me and Ion—

00:09:42.810 --> 00:09:45.180
You don't have a shoot today.

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:53.860
Looks like you lost your place here while you were out looking for Selectors.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:10:02.910
Oh, you poor thing! How ironic to see <i>you</i> fall to ruin before Iona does... right?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.290
I need to go.

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:09.830
Sore loser.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:16.220
I don't care if my life is ruined...

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:21.890
As long as I get to tear <i>your</i> life to shreds with my own hands!

00:10:23.510 --> 00:10:25.600
I guess it's game over for her.

00:10:30.940 --> 00:10:33.770
It doesn't look like you're running a fever.

00:10:33.770 --> 00:10:36.030
Do you still feel sick?

00:10:36.030 --> 00:10:39.570
My head still kinda hurts...

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:45.490
Well, let me call your teacher and tell them you'll stay home for the day.

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.750
I made Grandma worry...

00:10:52.750 --> 00:10:54.000
Ruu...

00:10:54.500 --> 00:10:57.090
<i>You were </i>enjoying<i> this!</i>

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:04.100
Why do I enjoy battling so much?

00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:09.850
I know what horrible things will happen if I go on... and yet...

00:11:09.850 --> 00:11:12.480
Don't cry, Ruu.

00:11:12.480 --> 00:11:16.800
You know, Tama likes seeing Ruu having fun in battles.

00:11:16.800 --> 00:11:19.900
So don't cry. We can have plenty of batt—

00:11:19.900 --> 00:11:21.320
Stop it!

00:11:21.700 --> 00:11:22.990
Ruu...

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.410
Hey, Kazuki? Let's go hang out sometime!

00:11:28.410 --> 00:11:29.710
Yeah, I'll go too!

00:11:30.210 --> 00:11:31.710
Sure, why not? Let's head out.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.330
Whoa, that's unusual for you.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:34.710
So, wanna grab some food?

00:11:34.710 --> 00:11:36.380
Yeah, sure.

00:11:36.380 --> 00:11:37.420
Let's go!

00:11:38.460 --> 00:11:39.630
Do you have a minute?

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:47.770
You know, you and Kazuki-kun don't really give off a good impression.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:51.640
People are kinda creeped out seeing you two together all the time.

00:11:52.020 --> 00:11:53.850
That was too blunt.

00:11:53.850 --> 00:11:58.400
Don't make that face. We're actually just worried about you two.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:11:59.360
Worried?

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:03.820
I feel bad for you two when I hear all the bad rumors,
so I wanted to give you some advice...

00:12:03.820 --> 00:12:05.410
What's that to you?

00:12:05.410 --> 00:12:06.450
Why do you care?

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:12.370
Well, to be honest, I'm only
concerned about Kazuki-kun.

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:14.630
I couldn't care less about you.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:18.960
I mean, I feel so sorry for Kazuki-kun when I see him being stalked by you.

00:12:18.960 --> 00:12:23.720
Yeah. You may not know, but Kazuki-kun is pretty popular.

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:26.300
Just because you're around, all the bad rumo—

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:28.850
What an attitude.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.140
Guess that means there's some truth to the rumors!

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:32.520
Now, now...

00:12:37.190 --> 00:12:38.690
Damn it...

00:12:39.070 --> 00:12:39.710
Yuzuki.

00:12:40.110 --> 00:12:41.190
Don't talk to me!

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:47.370
What's <i>wrong</i> with everyone?

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:49.930
<i>They're</i> the creeps...

00:12:49.930 --> 00:12:52.250
Hiya there!

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:57.360
You're a Selector, right?

00:12:57.540 --> 00:13:01.630
Yay! I finally met one! Wahoo!

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:07.390
It's so hard finding Selectors, you know?

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:11.180
Can you pretty pretty please
battle cute little Chiyori-chin?

00:13:11.180 --> 00:13:13.770
Let me give you a piece of advice.

00:13:13.770 --> 00:13:14.690
Huh?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:21.230
You're in for a lot of pain
if you lose in Selector battles.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.360
Yuzuki!

00:13:22.360 --> 00:13:24.360
Yes! I know!

00:13:26.030 --> 00:13:27.780
It's written right here!

00:13:28.990 --> 00:13:31.580
A WIXOSS... novelization?

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:32.330
Yup!

00:13:32.330 --> 00:13:34.250
If you lose three times,

00:13:34.250 --> 00:13:39.290
the WIXOSS factors expand inside your body
like a hot air balloon, and you go kaboom!

00:13:39.290 --> 00:13:40.710
And then you die, right?

00:13:41.130 --> 00:13:42.460
That's so scary!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:44.800
It's not lik—

00:13:44.800 --> 00:13:50.100
It's really cool that you still want to battle,
all for the sake of seeing your wish come true!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:57.270
I'm sorry. My girl here is a bit soft in the head, you know?

00:13:57.690 --> 00:13:59.650
That's so rude, Eldora!

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:02.270
At least I'm strong in battle!

00:14:02.270 --> 00:14:10.700
Anyway! My dear Selector-san, I'd like to offer my commemorative first battle to you!

00:14:11.200 --> 00:14:12.620
I...

00:14:15.040 --> 00:14:17.250
Oh come on, Kazuki-kun!

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:18.710
Honestly, it's not like that...

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.920
Hey, let's go to one more place!

00:14:20.920 --> 00:14:22.840
Well, uh, sure.

00:14:22.840 --> 00:14:25.800
There's so many things I want to ask you!

00:14:27.840 --> 00:14:30.340
Let's do this, okay? Please?!

00:14:31.510 --> 00:14:32.430
All right.

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.510
Yuzuki!

00:14:35.100 --> 00:14:36.520
Let's do this...

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:41.690
Yay! It's time to battle!

00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:50.160
I'm going to step out for a bit, so take a good rest, okay?

00:14:56.580 --> 00:15:01.710
<i>Why do I feel like... I've been looking for something all this time?</i>

00:15:04.590 --> 00:15:06.960
<i>If I can't have that something...</i>

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:11.890
<i>It feels like there's no reason to be alive. </i>

00:15:20.730 --> 00:15:23.440
I lost! I lost, darnit...!

00:15:23.440 --> 00:15:27.480
Goodness, she's strong!
Way stronger than you, Chiyori.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:30.110
So sorry to have bothered you there.

00:15:30.110 --> 00:15:32.160
Come on, Eldora!

00:15:32.160 --> 00:15:35.370
All great heroines lose their first battle!

00:15:35.950 --> 00:15:39.000
Yeah, right. That only happens in novels.

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.500
Let me give you this!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:43.380
And let's meet again, okay?

00:15:43.380 --> 00:15:45.750
Bye-bee!

00:15:51.300 --> 00:15:52.550
Yuzuki...

00:15:52.930 --> 00:15:55.180
I guess I won.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:15:56.180
Yeah.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:16:00.480
Losing three times means my wish won't come true.

00:16:01.020 --> 00:16:06.980
But there's no telling how many times I have to win for it to come true, right?

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:08.960
The conditions need to be met.

00:16:08.960 --> 00:16:13.950
"Conditions"? Yeah, there's the rub.

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:15.950
You'll probably tell me something later again...

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:22.330
I wonder what would happen if my wish were to be reversed?

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.500
Would I never be able to win Kazuki over?

00:16:27.290 --> 00:16:29.710
No, it has to be worse than that.

00:16:29.710 --> 00:16:34.130
Maybe Kazuki would hate me and I'd never be able to see him again.

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:40.350
I wonder where Kazuki went.

00:16:40.350 --> 00:16:41.600
Yuzuki.

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:44.770
Maybe he went to Momoka-san's place to pick up some cards.

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:47.480
The guys with him seemed new to the game.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:49.820
You think he's showing them all sorts of things?

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:50.980
Yuzuki, listen to me.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:56.660
Or maybe they went to the movies and
stopped by the food court for some matches.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:02.620
Or maybe they went for okonomiyaki and then they exchanged mail addresses—

00:17:02.620 --> 00:17:03.370
Yuzuki!

00:17:05.330 --> 00:17:06.540
I don't want this.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:12.920
I'd rather just disappear than see Kazuki taken from me!

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.310
Even if you're upset,
you should never say such a thing.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:22.270
I'm serious...

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:24.430
Hanayo-san, you're a liar!

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:30.770
But... I need you to have a chance for my wish to come true!

00:17:31.440 --> 00:17:35.450
I lost to Akira. But I was able to beat that girl, Chiyori!

00:17:35.860 --> 00:17:40.910
If I still have the chance to win...
if the chance to get Kazuki isn't gone yet...

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.830
If my wish isn't gone yet...

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:46.250
Then rather than having him taken from me...

00:17:46.960 --> 00:17:48.040
Yuzuki.

00:17:50.000 --> 00:17:54.590
I'm your LRIG. I'll follow you.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:56.630
No matter where.

00:18:00.640 --> 00:18:07.140
I don't think I asked for much back when I was living with my mother.

00:18:07.640 --> 00:18:11.320
She seemed so overwhelmed
even when she was all by herself.

00:18:12.150 --> 00:18:12.820
But...

00:18:13.480 --> 00:18:16.700
I don't know what Ruuko is thinking.

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:17.700
She's scary.

00:18:18.530 --> 00:18:23.700
I didn't know why I was scaring my mom... which scared me in turn, too.

00:18:24.750 --> 00:18:25.330
Kominato
Kominato

00:18:25.330 --> 00:18:28.460
I'm fine as long as I have Grandma and my brother with me.
Kominato
Kominato

00:18:28.870 --> 00:18:36.380
I didn't want to make anyone scared again, so I learned not to ask for much. I think...

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:37.840
And still...

00:18:41.510 --> 00:18:45.470
<i>You know, Tama likes seeing Ruu having fun in battles.</i>

00:18:49.480 --> 00:18:52.360
No... No, no!

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.450
The hell you're acting like you're the victim here?

00:18:59.860 --> 00:19:05.040
You enjoyed making me grovel before you.

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:11.000
Ruu-chan... Ruu-chan...

00:19:11.500 --> 00:19:12.750
Ruu-chan, wake up.

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:17.210
I'm sorry. I told her you were asleep.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.530
I'm sorry to bother you all of a sudden.

00:19:39.530 --> 00:19:44.700
Do you like parfaits? I ordered one on the off chance that you might like it.

00:19:44.700 --> 00:19:45.990
Thank you...

00:19:45.990 --> 00:19:49.790
Hitoe loves chestnut parfaits.
This one looks good!

00:19:50.330 --> 00:19:52.370
Maybe I should bring her here next time.

00:19:53.210 --> 00:19:54.290
Uhm...

00:19:56.420 --> 00:20:01.970
I found your number and Yuzuki-san's number in Hitoe's cell phone.

00:20:03.220 --> 00:20:06.930
You must think I'm a horrible mother, going through her daughter's phone.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:08.720
But, you see...

00:20:08.720 --> 00:20:11.810
That's the notebook Hitoe was keeping on battles—

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:12.890
You recognize this?

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.080
Y-Yes.

00:20:14.350 --> 00:20:18.900
The words written here...
Hitoe told me that she can't see them.

00:20:19.730 --> 00:20:22.780
She also said she doesn't know you girls.

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:27.490
<b>It made me happier than I've ever been before.
Sharing all the fun and happy words with everyone...</b>

00:20:27.490 --> 00:20:31.710
"Today, I bought matching pairs of scrunchies with Ruuko and Yuzuki."

00:20:32.160 --> 00:20:34.710
<i>"They looked really cute with them."</i>

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.210
<i>"They said I looked cute, too."</i>

00:20:39.210 --> 00:20:43.260
<i>"Sharing all the fun and
happy words with everyone..."</i>

00:20:43.260 --> 00:20:46.800
<i>"It made me happier than I've ever been before."</i>

00:20:46.800 --> 00:20:47.430
<b>Sharing all the fun and happy words with everyone...</b>

00:20:47.430 --> 00:20:50.270
<i>"Having friends really is nice."</i>
<b>Sharing all the fun and happy words with everyone...</b>

00:20:53.270 --> 00:20:56.860
She was so happy about having made friends.

00:20:57.440 --> 00:20:59.110
But now, she's...

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:04.110
Ruuko-san, if there's anything you know or may have noticed, can you please tell me?

00:21:04.110 --> 00:21:06.280
Even if it was just an argument you had with her...

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:09.780
Wait, I'm not trying to place the blame on you or anything, but it looks like something went off in her,

00:21:09.780 --> 00:21:11.700
and she's in shock, and...

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:17.040
Ruuko-san...?

00:21:18.290 --> 00:21:20.800
Hitoe lost three times...

00:21:22.420 --> 00:21:27.800
We didn't know that such a thing would happen if we lost...

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:34.310
We had fun... battling together was fun... and then...

00:21:34.310 --> 00:21:37.480
R-Ruuko-san? Calm down...

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.270
Ruuko-san?

00:21:43.740 --> 00:21:45.360
<i>I don't know...</i>

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:47.820
<i>What...</i>

00:21:49.370 --> 00:21:51.080
<i>I should do.</i>

